  "step_3": "The decision reason focuses on the difference in probabilities and prefers the lottery with the higher probability of a favorable outcome. While the individual acknowledges the similarity in probabilities, they do not base their decision on maximizing probability. Instead, they use the small probability difference to justify focusing on the higher payoff. There is no indication that the individual preferred the higher probability option (Lottery A) for probabilistic reasons; rather, their justification is outcome-based. Therefore, the decision reason—prioritizing higher probability—is not reflected in the individual’s stated reasoning. The information considered (probabilities) overlaps partially, but the rule (choosing based on higher probability) is not followed in the justification.",
  "final_assessment_score": 20
