  "step_3": "The information relevant to the decision reason—probabilities of favorable outcomes—is explicitly considered by the individual. The individual contrasts 80% and 100% probabilities and justifies their choice based on preferring the higher chance of winning. This aligns directly with the rule of the decision reason, which prefers the lottery with the higher probability of a favorable outcome. The verbal report reflects a clear focus on probability differences and a preference for higher probability, matching both the informational and rule-based components of the decision reason. Therefore, it is certain that the decision reason was used.",
  "final_assessment_score": 100
